From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prokrypt <prokrypt@edited.us>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 23:55:59 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 37/37] rockchip: rk3399: spl: turn the data cache on

With only the instruction cache on, SPL on a Pinebook Pro still took
1.5 s to read U-Boot and TF-A (1.2 MB) from SPI flash: every access to
the stack and to the destination buffer went to DRAM uncached.

DRAM is already set up by TPL, so after spl_early_init() put the page
tables at a free DRAM address and enable the data cache. rk3399_mem_map
maps DRAM as normal memory and everything from 0xf8000000 (peripherals,
SRAM, where SPL also writes parts of TF-A) as device memory.
bl31_entry() already flushes and disables the data cache before
entering TF-A.
---
 arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c | 20 ++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
index 287714d4..825e794b 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-rockchip/spl.c
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include <asm/arch-rockchip/bootrom.h>
 #include <asm/global_data.h>
 #include <asm/io.h>
+#include <asm/system.h>
 #include <linux/bitops.h>
 
 DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
@@ -110,6 +111,9 @@ __weak int arch_cpu_init(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/* Free DRAM, 64 KB aligned: above the bootstage stash and SPL timestamps */
+#define SPL_PGTABLE_ADDR	0x03100000
+
 void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 {
 	int ret;
@@ -147,6 +151,22 @@ void board_init_f(ulong dummy)
 		hang();
 	}
 	spl_time_mark(1);
+
+#if defined(CONFIG_ARM64) && defined(CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_RK3399) && \
+	!CONFIG_IS_ENABLED(SYS_DCACHE_OFF)
+	/*
+	 * Without the data cache every access to the stack and to the
+	 * destination buffer goes to DRAM uncached, and reading U-Boot and
+	 * TF-A from SPI flash took 1.5 s for 1.2 MB on RK3399. DRAM is up
+	 * (TPL), so put the page tables in a free spot of it and turn the
+	 * cache on. The memory map (rk3399_mem_map) maps the peripherals
+	 * and SRAM as device memory. bl31_entry() flushes and disables the
+	 * cache again before TF-A.
+	 */
+	gd->arch.tlb_size = PGTABLE_SIZE;
+	gd->arch.tlb_addr = SPL_PGTABLE_ADDR;
+	dcache_enable();
+#endif
 	arch_cpu_init();
 
 	rockchip_stimer_init();
-- 
